#
# SCENARIO PREMISE
#   Day 2, Wednesday 07:30. Players arrive as incident responders.
#   DarkVault ransomware hit Northgate General Hospital NHS Trust at 22:15
#   Monday night. The enterprise network and part of the clinical zone are
#   encrypted. Ward 7 central monitoring is offline. Patient safety is at
#   immediate risk.
#
# ROOM LAYOUT
#   ward_7  (start) → north → it_security_office → north → major_incident_room
#
# DEPLOYMENT
#   Copy this file to: BreakEscape/scenarios/sis01_healthcare/scenario.json.erb
#   Create a companion mission.json in that directory.
#   Ink story files go in:  scenarios/sis01_healthcare/ink/
#   VM content goes in:     Hacktivity VMs (see VM TODO comments below)
#
# ========================================================================
# IMPLEMENTATION STATUS
# ========================================================================
#
# IMPLEMENTED — no additional work required
#   siem_dashboard     lockType/type — SIEM alert triage (MG-01)
#   ransomware_display lockType      — infected workstation overlay (MG-05)
#
# PLACEHOLDER — functional stub in place; custom minigame needed
#   dual_auth_panel    → lockType:pin   (needs MG-11 dual_auth minigame)
#   backup_console     → lockType:pin   (needs MG-07 backup_recovery minigame)
#   bed2_pump_terminal → lockType:pin   (needs MG-08 infusion_pump minigame)
#   network_map_screen → readable text  (needs MG-04 interactive SVG map)
#   command_board      → readable text  (needs MG-12 auto-updating board)
#
# NOT YET BUILT — content or code required before this scenario can run
#   VM: northgate_vpn_logs    — Hacktivity VM for MG-06 (VPN log analysis)
#   VM: northgate_pump_mgmt   — Hacktivity VM for MG-09 (drug library integrity)
#   INK: 7 NPC story files    — see INK TODO comments on each NPC
#   SPRITES: ward room type   — room_office used as placeholder
#   SPRITES: clinical NPCs    — nurse, clinical engineer sprites needed
#
# ========================================================================
# ERB VARIABLES
# ========================================================================

require 'base64'

# Authorization codes — randomised per session so players cannot share solutions
itsec_pin    = rand(1000..9999).to_s    # Ravi's IT Security code (given via NPC dialogue)
clinical_pin = rand(1000..9999).to_s    # David's Clinical Engineering code (given after safety case assessment)
backup_pin   = rand(1000..9999).to_s    # Backup console placeholder PIN (replaced by MG-07)
